WEBVTT

00:00:00.046 --> 00:00:01.881
That creates an alignment gate.

00:00:02.264 --> 00:00:04.621
A gate is simply a point where we check whether a

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:06.687
condition is true before going on.

00:00:07.198 --> 00:00:10.043
Here, the condition is that the owner recognizes the

00:00:10.159 --> 00:00:12.214
readback as the intended experience.

00:00:12.655 --> 00:00:16.346
You can say, "Yes, that is right," or keep correcting it.

00:00:16.788 --> 00:00:19.911
This gate matters because architecture--the plan for how

00:00:19.969 --> 00:00:22.906
the pieces fit together--rests on the behavior we are

00:00:22.929 --> 00:00:23.835
trying to create.

00:00:24.276 --> 00:00:27.085
When a task is already agreed and authorized, the agent

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.127
should recognize that and continue from the current stage

00:00:30.173 --> 00:00:32.681
rather than force you to repeat the whole conversation.
